# What `just test` is allowed to send to the Docker daemon.
#
# NOTE this is NOT .gitignore — Docker does not read that file. Several paths
# below are already git-ignored and were still being baked into the image by
# `COPY . ${DOTFILES}` (test/Dockerfile), including real credentials:
#   .scratch/dotfiles/.kube/config
#   .scratch/dotfiles/.config/k3d/kubeconfig-catalyst-dev.yaml
#   .scratch/dotfiles/.config/op/config
#   .scratch/dotfiles/.config/argocd/config
# Those files stay on disk — they are simply never copied into a layer.
#
# Keep this a DENYLIST: the container genuinely needs most of the repo
# (flake.nix + flake.lock, home/, darwin/, hosts/, dotfiles/, test/), and an
# allowlist would silently starve the build the next time a module is added.

# ── vcs / build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.jj
result
result-*
*.hm-bak

# ── credentials and machine-local state ──────────────────────────────────────
# 278M pre-nix backup; carries kube/op/argocd configs. Kept on disk, never sent.
.scratch/
# rendered secret caches (op env), per-directory
.direnv/
**/.direnv/
# machine-local catalyst config: jira tenant, work email, private repo URLs
dotfiles/catalyst/config.yaml
# issue tracker db + credential key
.beads/
.claude/
.codex/

# ── bulk that has no business in the image ───────────────────────────────────
# 116M of node_modules/.venv build output from the demo flake
example/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
